@startuml investigation-sequence
!include _style.puml
' notes and messages on this diagram are prose; give them room before wrapping
skinparam wrapWidth 430
skinparam maxMessageSize 400
title One investigation, end to end

actor "Engineer" as H
participant "RunManager" as RM $accentFill
participant "Hooks\n<color:$muted>budget · guard · approval</color>" as HK $badFill
participant "Strands Agent\n<color:$muted>+ model provider</color>" as AG $accentFill
participant "12 @tools" as T $accentFill
participant "Metric store" as MS $greyFill
participant "Target repo\n<color:$muted>git worktrees</color>" as R $greyFill
participant "GitHub /\nSlack" as GH $greyFill

== Regression detected ==
H -> RM: investigate <repo>
note over H, RM $accentFill
  Also entered by `POST /api/runs` and the AgentCore entrypoint.
  `culprit watch` (nightly automation) enters here too — and is
  the only caller that sends the approval request to Slack.
end note
activate RM
RM -> AG: kickoff prompt\n(metric · repo · task)
activate AG
AG -> T: get_metric_history
T -> MS: read nightly history
MS --> T: <color:$bad>nightly (full config) f1 0.8301 → 0.6624</color>
T --> AG: good f665601 → bad 5022740
AG -> T: list_commits(window)
T -> R: git log
R --> T: 5 candidate commits

== Bisection ==
loop until one commit is isolated  ·  BudgetHook caps at CULPRIT_MAX_EXPERIMENTS
  AG -> T: run_experiment(sha, config)
  T -> R: git worktree add <sha[:12]>
  R --> T: metric for that commit
  T --> AG: <color:$bad>regressed</color> or <color:$good>clean</color>
  HK -[$warn]-> T: budget + loop guard
end
note over AG, R $goodFill
  recorded churn demo (offline policy): **4** experiments isolate **c249462**
  — 2 calibration (last good, first bad) + 2 bisection steps.
  A 5th, below, verifies the fix: **5 experiments in total**.
end note

AG -> T: show_commit + read_file
T --> AG: root cause in the diff

== Fix ==
AG -> T: start_fix
T -> R: branch culprit/fix-<run_id> + worktree
AG -> T: edit_file (churn/features.py)
AG -> T: run_experiment(fix branch)  ← the 5th
T --> AG: <color:$good>fast config f1 0.7027 → 0.8111 — back to the good-commit value</color>
AG -> T: write_file (guard test)
AG -> T: run_tests
T --> AG: <color:$good>tests pass</color>

group$badFill $badFill  APPROVAL GATE  —  a human must say yes
  AG -> T: open_pull_request
  activate T $badFill
  HK -[$bad]-> RM: **interrupt**\n"culprit-approval:open_pull_request"
  deactivate T
  deactivate AG
  RM -> RM: status = awaiting_human\npersist pending_interrupts
  RM -[$bad]-> H: approval request\n(dashboard · SSE `interrupt` event)
  note over H, RM $badFill
    **The agent stops here.** No PR is opened without a human.
    The process may exit — the state is on disk.
  end note

  ... run paused — resume from any process, any time ...

  H -[$good]-> RM: approve / reject
  activate RM
  RM -> AG: replay interruptResponse\ninto a fresh Agent (same session)
  activate AG
end

== Land & report ==
alt approved
  AG -> T: open_pull_request (resumed)
  T -> GH: PR + notification
  GH --> T: <color:$good>PR opened</color>
else rejected
  HK -[$bad]-> AG: cancel_tool — "do not retry,\nfinish with a summary"
  note over AG, GH $badFill
    **No PR.** The fix branch and its worktree stay on disk, reviewable.
  end note
end
RM -> AG: report prompt\nstructured_output_model = IncidentReport
AG --> RM: IncidentReport
deactivate AG
RM -> RM: report.md · report.json\nstatus = completed
RM --> H: incident report
deactivate RM

legend right
|<back:$badFill>    </back>| gate — regression · hooks · human approval |
|<back:$goodFill>    </back>| verified fix |
|<back:$accentFill>    </back>| agent path |
endlegend
@enduml
